<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-204] SparkJLineCompletion (used by SparkInterpreter) does not return completion suggestions. </title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-204</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Although the SparkJLineCompletion receives the  complete buffer and correct cursor &lt;a href=&quot;#**&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;**&lt;/a&gt; it does not produce any results. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The JLine competition (used internally) operates on a single word and not entire buffer.  So the interpreter may have to filter in only the selected word(s) and pass those to the  SparkJLineCompletion. This approach works for related PostgreSQL autocompletion implementation. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;#42;&amp;#42; &lt;a name=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Note that this issue is blocked by &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-196&quot; title=&quot;The Auto-completion functionality is broken &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-196&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-196&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. One need to apply &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/180&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/180&lt;/a&gt; to allow the buffer and cursor to be passed to the interpteter. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
